### W5.5 · Fix: md() no longer sees an indented fence, a regression in chat and task prose
Parent: W5.4
Status: open
Approach: In `scripts/web/index.html`, `md(raw)` splits on `/(?:^|
)```[^
]*(?:
|$)/` (changed in W5.3/W5.4 so an inline triple backtick does not open a fence). The pattern needs the fence flush at the line start, so a fence indented under a list item (`- step
  ```
  code
  ```), which agent replies and task prose use all the time, no longer splits: the code is not drawn in `<pre>`, the ``` lines show as typed, and `inline` runs over the code lines (so `**` and backticks inside it are styled). Before W5.4 this rendered as a block, so chat output changed, against W5.1's "chat output is unchanged". Fix: allow leading spaces or tabs on both the opening and closing fence line (`/(?:^|
)[ 	]*```[^
]*(?:
|$)/`), keep the inline-triple-backtick case literal, and settle it with a new case in the `markdown` flow of `scripts/ui_flows.mjs`: an indented fence in a list item gives `<pre>` with the code escaped. Run the regex over the sample in Python or node, as no browser exists here.
